AB  - The sixth-generation wireless communication $(6 G)$ promises advancements in speed, latency, and connectivity to facilitate revolutionary technology like holographic communication, extensive AI, and Internet of Everything (IoE). Such breakthroughs come with sophisticated cyber security issues like ultra-dynamic attack surfaces, decentralized device systems, and quantum-vulnerable encryption protocols. To counter these challenges, this paper investigates the application of blockchain technology and quantum computing as solutions for 6G cyber security improvement. Blockchain provides a tamper-proofed, decentralized system that guarantees data integrity, secure authentication, and transparent access control among heterogeneous devices. However, quantum computing also provides solutions such as post-quantum cryptography (PQC) and quantum key distribution (QKD) that can enhance communication resilience against quantum and conventional assaults. Β© 2025 IEEE.
