AB  - The advent of quantum computing poses significant security risks to blockchainbased healthcare systems since it can undermine established cryptographic techniques like RSA and ECC. Using Kyber for key exchange, Falcon for authentication, and a code-based Key Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) for increased security, this article suggests a quantum-resistant blockchain system for safe healthcare data transmission. To guarantee data integrity, confidentiality, and tamper resistance, patient medical records are encrypted and kept on a blockchain. When compared to conventional methods, performance evaluation shows lower latency, stronger security, and effective blockchain storage. The suggested framework offers a scalable, future-ready defense against quantum attacks for private health information. Β© 2026 IEEE.
