AB  - The significance of safe and cooperative digital asset management systems has been brought to light by the emergence of cryptocurrencies and decentralized finance (DeFi). By incorporating several parties in the administration and approval of transactions, multi-party crypto vaults offer a means to guarantee distributed control, privacy, and fault tolerance. The two main methods that support these vaults-Multi-Signature (Multi-Sig) and Multi-Party Computation (MPC),are reviewed in this study. While multi-sig schemes provide rapid scalable solutions for real-time applications, MPC provides robust privacy and security by permitting encrypted calculations without disclosing private keys. Furthermore, fault tolerance techniques like social recovery and time-locked protocols, as well as key management models like split-key and blockchain-based approaches, guarantee that vault systems continue to be safe and functional even in the event of participant failure. This paper recommends MPC as the optimal approach for high-security, privacy-sensitive applications, such as institutional custody and financial systems, while outlining avenues for future research, including post-quantum cryptography and latency reduction in MPC protocols. Β© 2025 IEEE.
