AB  - The diversity of digital capabilities has been improved by new cloud-native, microservices, DevSecOps, and IoT software designs, which have also designed a path to cyber threats. Outdated security tools like firewalls and signature-driven recognition are not very effective against ransomware, insider threats, phishing attacks, sophisticated persistent threats and zero-day attacks. The practice of AI can be in the zones of intrusion prevention, malware detection, phishing resistance, insider monitoring, and IoT and autonomous platforms security. These concerns increase major ethical alarms to software engineers who must confirm that the AI systems are transparent, accountable, and fair. XAI and privacy-sensitive models, as well as compliance with such regulations as GDPR and the EU AI Act, provide muchneeded protection. Future secure AI developments in cybersecurity include secure AI innovations such as federated learning, blockchain-based AI, and quantum-safe algorithms. Β© 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
