AB  - Because of sophisticated question paper fraud and leaks, educational institutions face significant challenges in maintaining the integrity of examinations. Conventional security techniques that concentrate on centralized systems have shown themselves susceptible to internal threats and illegal access. This paper presents a blockchain-based system that transforms examination security through smart contracts and distributed ledger technology. Our approach builds a private permissioned blockchain with multi-signature authentication, time-locked releases, and quantum-resistant encryption using Hyperledger Fabric. Our approach builds a private permissioned blockchain with multi-signature authentication, time-locked releases, and quantum-resistant encryption using Hyperledger Fabric. Real-time audit logging, geographic access restrictions, and fragment-based storage are some of the major innovations. Unauthorized access attempts have decreased by 99.9% and administrative overhead has decreased by 60% in pilot installations. The framework provides educational institutions with a safe and scalable solution, with the potential to integrate AI and enhance evaluation capabilities. This study significantly advances educational technology by addressing significant security concerns and enabling efficient exam administration.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
