AB  - The Energy Internet (EI) has revolutionized the generation, distribution, and consumption of energy by leveraging the Internet of Things (IoT). However, it faces significant security challenges, particularly in light of advancements in quantum computing. To address these challenges, this paper proposes a combined approach of post-quantum cryptography and blockchain technology to enhance security and authentication in the EI. The proposed solution aims to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of critical information, thereby strengthening the resilience of the energy grid. We validate the security of the proposed protocol using BAN logic. Furthermore, simulations conducted with the Proverif security tool demonstrate the protocol's effectiveness against various threats. The research presented in this paper contributes to the development of a secure and sustainable future for the Energy Internet.  Β© 2023 IEEE.
